# --------------------------------------------
# Output Files (Generated) -- the six sample newsletters in output/ are tracked
# on purpose: index.html links all of them as the GitHub Pages showcase, and
# the README points at WEEK21. Reports, drafts and previews are regenerable.
# --------------------------------------------
output/stats_report_week*.json
output/stats_report_week*.md
output/looking_ahead_week*.json
output/WEEK*_NEWSLETTER.pdf
output/player_card_preview.html

# --------------------------------------------
# Assets - Weekly Drafts
# --------------------------------------------
assets/WEEK*_DRAFT.md

# --------------------------------------------
# Data Files - Weekly Inputs
# --------------------------------------------
data/waivers_week*.txt
data/weeklycontextinput_week*.json

# --------------------------------------------
# Data Files - Excel (Large)
# --------------------------------------------
data/PLAYERLOG.xlsx
data/LINEUPS.xlsx
data/LEAGUEHISTORY.xlsx

# --------------------------------------------
# Config Files - Dynamic State
# --------------------------------------------
config/ROSTERS.json
config/RECORDS.json

# --------------------------------------------
# Integrity baseline (machine-specific)
# --------------------------------------------
config/.file_baselines.json

# --------------------------------------------
# Historical Data -- TRACKED ON PURPOSE
# --------------------------------------------
# data/historical/ is the permanent, append-only record: nine-plus seasons of
# standings, matchups, drafts, trades, and per-game player logs. It is NOT
# regenerable in practice -- Yahoo's API is the only upstream source, old
# league keys go stale, and the season reset truncates the working PLAYERLOG.
# These files are committed so the record has offsite, versioned backup.
# Do not re-ignore them without arranging another backup first.
#
# (Rolling backups are still ignored -- see "Large backup files" below.)

# --------------------------------------------
# Keep These in Repo (Templates/Config)
# --------------------------------------------
# !data/PLAYERLIST.xlsx        # Player projections - keep if sharing
# !config/SCHEDULE.json        # League schedule structure - keep
# !config/INJURY_OVERRIDES.json # Can keep as example
# !data/nba_schedule_*.json    # NBA schedule - keep
# !templates/newsletter_template.md # Template - definitely keep
# !*.example                   # Example files - keep

# --------------------------------------------
# Logs and Temp Files
# --------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp
*.cache
.cache/
.pytest_cache/
pytest-cache-files-*/

# --------------------------------------------
# Jupyter Notebooks (if any)

# --------------------------------------------
# Large backup files
# --------------------------------------------
data/historical/*_BACKUP.json
data/historical/*_BACKUP.xlsx

# --------------------------------------------
# Cowork backup directory
# --------------------------------------------
_backups/

# Review/repair artifacts (not part of the engine)
PROJECT_REVIEW_REPORT.html
THESIS_DEFENSE_REPORT.html
_recovery/

# State-migration archive (contains credentials -- never commit)
newsletter_state.zip
